["LARN stands for…","Reference Intake Levels for Nutrients and Energy","Recommended Levels of Adult Nutrition","Regional Assessment of Nutritional Requirements","Reference Levels of Average Nutrients","p.12."],
["LARN are the official reference values for…","the Italian population","the European population","hospital patients only","athletes","p.12."],
["LARN were formulated by…","a committee of experts of the Italian society of human nutrition (SINU)","the WHO","CREA only","the Ministry of Agriculture","p.12."],
["LARN values correspond to…","higher values than average needs, with a safety margin","exact average needs","minimum survival intakes","maximum tolerable intakes","p.12."],
["LARN are more valid for…","groups than for individuals, except energy needs","individuals only","patients only","children only","p.12."],
["LARN should be met over…","the weekly diet","a single day","a single meal","one month","p.12–13."],
["LARN safeguard the health of about…","97.5% of the healthy population","50% of the population","100% including patients","80% of adults","p.13."],
["LARN were formulated for…","healthy individuals, by age and sex groups","patients with chronic disease","only the elderly","only children","p.12."],
["Which is a use of LARN?","Support nutritional labeling and health claims","Diagnose malnutrition","Dose drugs","Screen for eating disorders","p.12."],
["A balanced diet must include…","fibre, vitamins, minerals, water and variety across the day","only macronutrients","only fruit and vegetables","only low-calorie foods","p.12."]
