a:"<ul><li><b>IDF 2005 (table, p.22):</b> central obesity — waist circumference with ethnicity-specific values (Europids ≥94 cm men / ≥80 cm women; South Asian, Chinese, Japanese ≥90 / ≥80; or assumed if BMI &gt;30) — <b>plus 2</b> of: triglycerides ≥150 mg/dl; HDL &lt;40 men / &lt;50 women; BP ≥130/85 mmHg; impaired fasting glucose.</li><li><b>Diet (5.2):</b> 5–10% weight loss in year 1 (BMI &lt;25); low-GI diet, refined sugars/white flour ↓, legumes, whole grains, vegetables ↑; sodium &lt;2 g/day; saturated fat &lt;10% (&lt;7%), cholesterol &lt;300 mg/day, fibre 25–40 g/day; fish ≥2×/week and ω-3; Mediterranean/DASH pattern; 30–60 min activity, smoking cessation.</li></ul><p><b>Note:</b> the IDF glucose threshold is ambiguous in the table (IFG, “&gt;100 mg/dl”); the bank’s 2009 Joint Interim Statement question is not covered.</p>",
